Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 19:27:34 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix: detect images by content block, patch the two vendor
 gaps
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Two things the gateway still gets wrong after 33841d5:

- wantsVision searched the serialized request for the literal
  "image_url", so a plain-text message that mentions the field name
  was treated as an image: `text` mode answered 400, and `auto`
  wasted a vision model on it. Walk the structured content blocks
  instead (image / image_url / input_image), covering OpenAI chat,
  Responses and Anthropic shapes.

- vendor/ (third-party, re-downloaded by setup) has two defects the
  standalone gateway exposes: `json()` sends no CORS headers, so a
  browser front end passes preflight and then has its real response
  blocked; and auth accepts only `authorization: Bearer …` and
  `x-api-key`, so clients that send the Azure-style `api-key` header
  get a 401. scripts/patch-vendor.mjs applies both idempotently
  (npm run patch, --check, forward.js.orig backup) and is safe to
  re-run after setup.
